--TEST--
An event stream's message answers the name it was published under as a `string` and what was published as `mixed`, so the value reaches no typed position unchecked — `rule:concurrency/a-connection-is-a-loop`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Every message an event stream receives is a bus delivery, so `topic()` is a
// `string` and never `null`: there is no second kind of message for a reader
// to answer `null` about, and the `?` the sibling class costs its callers is
// not owed here.
//
// `value()` is whatever the publisher put there, which is `mixed` and is
// refused where a `string` is what the position takes -- the reading a decoded
// document already gets, and the one that keeps a published value from
// reaching a typed position on the strength of who sent it.
class Feed {
    public static function describe(Core\Sse\Message $msg): string {
        echo $msg->topic(), "\n";
        return $msg->value();
    }
}
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0403]: this method declares `string` but returns `mixed`
   --> case.nvs:14:16
   |
14 |         return $msg->value();
   |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ this is `mixed`

error: aborting due to 1 error
